# Pages & Routing

## Pages Organization (`/src/pages/`)

### Principles
1. All page components in `/src/pages/`
2. Organize by domain/module (`mine/`, `work/`, `common/`)
3. Use kebab-case for folder names
4. Main page is `index.vue`

### Example Structure
```
/src/pages/
├── index.vue           # Home (tab bar)
├── login.vue          # Login
├── work/index.vue     # Work (tab bar)
├── mine/
│   ├── index.vue      # Mine (tab bar)
│   ├── info/
│   │   ├── index.vue
│   │   └── edit.vue
│   └── setting/index.vue
```

## Routing Configuration (`pages.json`)

### Page Configuration

**⚠️ CRITICAL**: The **first page** in the array is the **entry page** (app startup page).

```json
{
  "pages": [
    {
      "path": "pages/login",  // ⚠️ FIRST PAGE = ENTRY PAGE
      "style": {
        "navigationBarTitleText": "登录"
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "pages/index",  // Other pages
      "style": {
        "navigationBarTitleText": "首页"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Page Order Rules**:
- ⚠️ **First page is the entry page** (app starts here)
- ⚠️ **ALWAYS append new pages to the end** - do NOT insert at position 0
- Inserting at position 0 will change the app's entry point!

**Adding New Pages**:
```json
{
  "pages": [
    { "path": "pages/login" },  // ⚠️ DO NOT INSERT HERE
    // ... existing pages
    {
      "path": "pages/new-feature/index",  // ✅ ADD AT THE END
      "style": {
        "navigationBarTitleText": "New Feature"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

